    "bio": "a Representative from Massachusetts; born in Rehoboth, Mass., September 3, 1739; attended the common schools; served in the Revolutionary War; was an innkeeper; served in the Massachusetts state senate 1787-1791; member of the Massachusetts state house of representatives in 1792, 1793, 1797, and 1798; elected as a Democratic Republican to the Sixth through Ninth Congresses (March 4, 1799-March 3, 1807); died in Rehoboth, Mass., January 6, 1812; interment in Old Cemetery, Rumford, East Providence, R.I.",
